{"type":"message","id":"47734ec7","parentId":"d9ade43d","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:55:34.842Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the tools available, I don't see a `sessions_spawn` tool directly. Let me check if there's another way to spawn agents. I see references to `sessions_spawn` in the subagent context but it's not listed as a tool.\n\nLet me check the available tools again - I have:\n- read\n- write\n- exec\n- process\n- web_search\n- web_fetch\n- message\n\nHmm, there's no `sessions_spawn` or `subagents` tool in my available tools list. Let me check if I can use the `exec` tool to run `openclaw` commands that might spawn agents.\n\nLooking at the OpenClaw CLI, I see:\n- `openclaw agent` - Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n- `openclaw acp` - Run an ACP bridge (for ACP harness sessions like codex/claudecode/gemini)\n\nBut the task says to use `sessions_spawn(agentId: \"search-agent\")` which suggests there should be a way to spawn subagents. \n\nLet me check if there's a subagent skill or if I can access agents list.\n\nActually, looking at the context more carefully, it mentions:\n- \"Use the `subagents` tool to steer, kill, or do an on-demand status check for your spawned subagents.\"\n- \"`agents_list` and `subagents` apply to OpenClaw sub-agents (`runtime: \"subagent\"`)\"\n\nBut I don't have these tools listed. Let me try using exec to interact with the OpenClaw CLI and see if I can spawn agents that way.\n\nActually, I need to re-read the subagent context:\n\"Sub-Agent Spawning: You CAN spawn your own sub-agents for parallel or complex work using `sessions_spawn`.\"\n\nBut sessions_spawn is not in my tool list. This is confusing. Let me check if perhaps the tool is available under a different name or if I need to use exec.\n\nLooking at the system prompt again: \"Tool availability (filtered by policy): Tool names are case-sensitive. Call tools exactly as listed.\"\n\nAnd my available tools are: read, write, exec, process, web_search, web_fetch, message\n\nSo sessions_spawn is NOT available to me. This means I cannot follow the task as specified because I don't have the ability to spawn other agents.\n\nWait, let me re-read the task:\n\"🔴 强制要求：必须委托给其他 Agent\"\n\"步骤 1：使用 `sessions_spawn(agentId: \"search-agent\")` 调研...\"\n\nBut I don't have sessions_spawn as an available tool. Let me try to see if I can accomplish this through exec commands or if there's another way.\n\nActually, I notice the task mentions \"search-agent\", \"code-agent\", \"test-agent\" but when I look at the available skills, I don't see these listed. Let me check if these agents exist.\n\nLet me try `openclaw agents list` to see what agents are configured.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"让我检查可用的 agents："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-4e5b5b8c35dd4793b54c477757b02a02","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agents list"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":21,"output":1265,"cacheRead":11119,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12405,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772423716976}}
